2. Mistakes / Issues

Header issues:

Two <h1> tags used (restaurant name + menu heading), not ideal for SEO/accessibility.

Hamburger/nav toggle alignment may break on very small screens; spacing and logo size need adjustment.


Responsive design issues:

Fixed margin (margin-left:100px) and large logo heights affect small screen alignment.

.controls section may not fully scale on mobile.


Accessibility:

Missing ARIA labels for navigation toggle.

Some alt attributes for images are missing or inconsistent (soda.jpg, tea.jpg).


CSS styling issues:

Border-radius of 1px on cards is almost invisible.

Footer links green on goldenrod reduce readability.


Content errors:

Spelling inconsistency (custurd instead of custard).


Code cleanliness:

Commented-out header code remains in HTML, which can confuse future maintenance.

3. Guidelines & Areas of Improvement

Remove all commented-out or unused code for cleaner structure.

Use one main <h1> per page; convert restaurant name to <h2> or <span>.

Replace fixed spacing/margins with Flexbox alignment for better responsive behavior.

Reduce logo size and make it responsive using max-height in media queries.

Add complete and descriptive alt text for all images to improve accessibility.

Add ARIA attributes for mobile nav toggle (aria-label="Toggle Navigation").

Ensure consistent spelling in content (custard) and unify capitalization across headings.

Adjust footer link colors to match theme and ensure readability (e.g., whitesmoke text).

Optimize JavaScript by using class-based toggles for search/filter instead of inline display:block/none for better performance with large menus.

